A||N||8||Dan87GT||v6 fuel pressure @ 20psi||||1||
Z||000000||Dan87GT||06-17-2000||12:16 PM||||I am having a problem with my 86se, it is missing in the lower rpm range, I checked the fuel pressure and it is at 20 psi, could this be the problem - a bad fuel pump?? I already changed the filter.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||terryk||06-17-2000||12:20 PM||||Could be the regulator. Pull the vacuum line from the regulator and measure it.<P>After that, it sounds like the pump, strainer screen is clogged or the pulse dampener in the tank is leaking.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Dan87GT||06-18-2000||07:38 AM||||Thanks, its was the fuel pump. I was stumped because it was running fine at the upper RPM range and terrible at the lower, I expected the opposite. Its running great now!||||reg||1
Z||000003||jlruiz67||06-21-2000||01:01 PM||||Did you use a stock fuel pump or after market? I like to know if there is any better alternative to the stock fuel pump.<BR>Thanks||||reg||6
Z||000004||Dan87GT||06-21-2000||01:05 PM||||I used a stock replacement pump, I was completely frustrated at the time because I had just topped the tank off with gas, making the pump change a pain. I know the Fiero Store sells Holly pumps.||||reg||1
Z||000005||80's BOY||06-21-2000||01:07 PM||||in a thread awhile back someone said to use an iroc z fuel pump, so i'm trying that. it was only 60 bucks new.||||reg||7
Z||000006||terryk||06-21-2000||01:59 PM||||I don't see any reason to go to a bigger pump unless you go to a bigger engine, but NAPA sells the 89 Turbo Trans Am pump for around $55 (unless they caught on).||||reg||1
Z||000007||triker||06-21-2000||04:23 PM||||If you were even considering a larger engine at some point in the future, wouldn't it make sense to put in a larger pump now if your orginal went south?  Other than a little more electricity to push the extra volumn back through the by-pass line, it shouldn't hurt anything.||||reg||1
